// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-META-ONE1=A / D-FACT-LAW1=B: marker vocabulary, effect roots, and fact law
//RS //! rows are written as Prelude declarations, and Rust keeps no copy.
//RS //!
//RS //! The marker guard proves the real Jet parser reads the same file the
//RS //! compiler's registry reader reads, and agrees on every name, every parameter,
//RS //! and every site — so the small reader in `jet-foundation` (which sits below
//RS //! the parser in the crate graph and cannot call it) can never drift from the
//RS //! language. The fact guard checks both law columns against the one registry.
//RS //! The source scan rejects second Rust copies.
//RS 
